  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$f(x)=\\frac{x+3}{x-2}$\n$\\because \\quad f(x)$ is not defined for $x=2$\ni.e. domain of $f(x)$ is $\\mathrm{R}-\\{2\\}$\n$\\therefore l=2$\nNow, $y=\\frac{x+3}{x-2}$\n$x y-2 y=x+3$\n$x(y-1)=2 y+3$\n$x=\\frac{2 y+3}{y-1}$\n$y$ can take any value except $y=1$\nCo-domain $=\\mathrm{R}-\\{1\\}$\n$m=1$\n$3 l+2 m=3(2)+2(1)=8$",
    "image": null
